  (text "2x 18650 in PARALLEL (single-cell TP4056 rating). TP4056 module: USB-C on the module, IN+ pad = VBUS (tap it), IN- NC.\nDIODE OR-ING (charge and load paths separated): D3 VBUS->VSYS, D4 cell->VSYS. USB present -> VSYS = 5V-Vf ~4.7V, D4 is\nreverse-biased (cell max 4.2V-Vf = 3.9V), so the load runs from USB and the cell sees only the TP4056 charge loop (correct\nCC/CV termination, boots with a dead cell). USB absent -> D4 conducts, VSYS = VBAT-Vf. Both must be Schottky (SS34: Vf ~0.3V\nat 1A, 3A rated) so the battery path loses as little as possible; never use 1N4007 here.\nCost of the diode path: ~0.3V and ~0.3W at 1A lost on battery power, and the boost sees a 0.3V lower input (brownout headroom\nshrinks). If that bites, swap D4 for a P-MOSFET ideal diode (AO3401, gate to VBUS, 100k to GND).\nUSB budget: charger (1A, Rprog=1.2k) + load share one 5V input -> use a 2A+ adapter or raise Rprog (3k = 400mA). Module USB-C\nneeds CC pull-downs (5.1k) or a C-to-C cable gives no VBUS. Set MT3608 to 5.0V BEFORE connecting the devkit.\nPlanned UVLO (not built): insert between D4 cathode and VSYS so a drained cell cuts off instead of brownout-looping." (at 25.4 238.76 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "438c3f49-ec61-4079-8a6f-b31e7dcad86f"))
  (sheet_instances (path "/" (page "1")))
